<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Awami League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bangladesh Awami League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Awami League is a political party of Bangladesh, founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a> in 1949 as a rival to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">Muslim League</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</a> it campaigned for Bengali autonomy, won the 1970 general election and led the independence struggle of 1971. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-hasina">Sheikh Hasina</a>, it governed from 1996 to 2001 and from 2009 until she was forced from office in 2024, after which its activities were banned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/awami-league.jpg" alt="Awami League" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nirvik12 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%A6%AC%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%82%E0%A6%B2%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%A6%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%B6_%E0%A6%86%E0%A6%93%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BC%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%AE%E0%A7%80_%E0%A6%B2%E0%A7%80%E0%A6%97%E0%A7%87%E0%A6%B0_%E0%A6%AC%E0%A7%8D%E0%A6%AF%E0%A6%BE%E0%A6%9C.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
